>> title: Mayonnaise
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: eggs, emulsion, sandwich, no-cook
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: mayo
>> servings: 8
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the oil goes in drop by drop and an emulsion that breaks does not re-form by whisking harder: it has to be started again in a clean bowl with a fresh yolk and the broken batch beaten back in. Raw yolk also means it is a fridge item, not a counter one
>> step.1: whisk together
>> step.2: drizzle in drop by drop
>> step.3: whisk in
>> step.4: loosen and season

Whisk @egg yolk{1%large}(at room temperature) with @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, and @lemon juice{2%tsp} in a bowl set on a damp towel.

Drizzle @neutral oil{1%cup}(240 mL) into @&(~1)yolk{} drop by drop at first, whisking constantly, then in a thin thread once it thickens.

Whisk @white wine vinegar{1%tsp} into @&(~1)mayonnaise{}.

Loosen @&(~1)mayonnaise{} with @cold water{2%tsp} and @white pepper{1/8%tsp}.
